.graph_engine_runs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Biometric runtime data - NEVER commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Face crops of employees AND of unidentified passers-by who never consented to
# being recorded. Special-category personal data under the DPDP Act / GDPR, and
# git history is permanent - a later `git rm` does not remove it. These are
# written continuously by the camera pipeline and are on a retention clock
# (attendance_snapshot.prune_snapshots / unknown_faces.purge_older_than), so
# they are transient runtime state, not source.
**/data/attendance_snapshots/
**/data/unknown_faces/
**/data/enroll_review/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs - NEVER commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs written before main.RedactCredentialsFilter existed contain the DVR
# password in plaintext (app-run.log.err held 30,719 copies of it). They also
# carry employee names and other PII from the recognition trace.
*.log
*.log.err
**/logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored third-party model source - NEVER commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# third_party/AdaFace is a CLONE (it has its own .git) weighing 1.2 GB, of which
# 1.19 GB is the same 596 MB checkpoint stored twice - adaface_ir50_webface4m.ckpt
# sits at the repo root AND under pretrained/. Both are far past GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit, and a nested .git cannot be committed as ordinary files anyway.
# Fetch it at setup time instead; see the AdaFace upstream repo.
**/third_party/AdaFace/

# Staging folder for face-enrolment photos. Biometric data - same rule as
# data/unknown_faces and data/attendance_snapshots above: never committed.
enrol_drop/

# CCTV V2 measurement clips: frames of identifiable people. Never commit.
data/cctv_v2_*/

# ── Large model artifacts: NOT source, and unpushable ──────────────────────
# A 505 MB push timed out with "RPC failed; HTTP 408" — and even with more
# patience GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100 MB, so these could never land.
# Both are DERIVED or DOWNLOADED, so committing them buys nothing and costs
# every future clone the same half gigabyte forever (git keeps blobs in history
# even after a delete).
#
#   adaface_ir50_webface4m.onnx  166 MB  regenerate:
#       python scripts/export_adaface_onnx.py
#       (also re-runs the equivalence check against the .ckpt)
#
#   weights/clip/ViT-B-32.pt     338 MB  a published CLIP weight; re-download
#       it from the upstream project rather than versioning it here.
#
# The deploy path does not need these in git: scripts/package-for-server.ps1
# copies models/ straight from the working tree.
#
# NOTE: models/yolo11*.pt|onnx and osnet_*.onnx are already tracked from earlier
# commits that are on origin. They are deliberately NOT ignored here — an ignore
# rule does not untrack a file, and rewriting pushed history to drop them is a
# separate, coordinated job.
weights/
Attendance Management/backend/models/adaface_ir50_webface4m.onnx

# Working artifacts that got committed by accident
Attendance Management/backend/gallery_clean_plan.json
*.tsbuildinfo
